  "note": "Ledgerline as an emitted-light terminal rather than a printed accounting pad. Same object spine: one transaction row, line 47 of the export, carried through four states without ever dying. The look changes the physics, not the story. A selected line is marked by a bloom behind it and by its own rising emission, never by a rectangle, because on a near-black ground a filled box reads as a hole punched in the screen rather than as a highlight. Colour keeps the paper cut's meaning: ember is raw and owed, lime is parsed and filed, so the row literally changes colour as the software understands it. A low CRT overlay and a slow continuous camera drift carry the room.",
